    paragraph(design, 'Registration is not universally idempotent.', '**Registration state and entry point (Serp confirmation, 2026-10-03):** XML ActionRegisterTrigger does nothing if the trigger is already registered. Once the full trigger has completed, it is no longer registered and can be registered again. Lua registration can instead register the same trigger multiple times concurrently; one GUID does not guarantee one active instance. Serp considers self-registration directly from the trigger\'s own action **possible but unconfirmed**; use ActionResetTrigger or the embedded ResetTrigger for that repetition. Do not infer the completion boundary during an executing action list from the ability to register after full completion. Earlier circular-registration failures retain their exact test context.')
    paragraph(design, 'Registered and fired trigger state persists', '**Code snapshot on registration (Serp confirmation, 2026-10-03):** registration captures the code present at that moment as the trigger\'s saved definition. An already-registered instance retains that snapshot; editing XML does not update it in place. A later fresh registration captures the current code, including changed conditions/actions. XML ActionRegisterTrigger on an already-registered instance does nothing, so it does not refresh that snapshot: an unregister/re-register workflow must actually reach a fresh registration. This confirms the previously open saved-code-refresh mechanism, without promising replay or migration of completed rewards, missed events or already-applied effects. Adding a ResetTrigger to an already-completed GUID does not retroactively execute it. A new GUID may still be useful for an explicitly guarded migration. Do not reuse a historical GUID merely because it is now "free" or used as text.')
    replace(design, 'Re-registration and nested optional-depth boundaries remain open; passing offline patches does not resolve them.', 'Serp also confirms XML-versus-Lua registration and code snapshots; nested optional-depth is very likely clarified, while direct self-registration remains unconfirmed. Passing offline patches adds no runtime proof.')
